	(text "TCAN-27 Data Logger. Teensy 4.1 on female headers. 12V in, reverse-polarity P-FET (Q1), TVS (D3), OKI-78SR-5 to Teensy VIN through D1.\nMCP3208 runs on 3V3 (Teensy pins are not 5V tolerant): sensors 0-5V divided by (2.2k+470)/4.7k to about 3.2V, D4-D7 clamp to 3V3."
		(at 20.32 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "047b3242-5fc4-4ac0-8356-a2a7e62e92d0")
	)
	(text "OPEN CHECKS before building: (1) PJRC says do not power VIN while USB is connected: cut the VUSB-VIN pad pair on the Teensy bottom, or never connect both.\n(2) OKI-78SR datasheet absolute-max input NOT verified. D3 is 1.5KE24A (clamp ~33V). The owned 1.5KE36A clamps ~50V, which may exceed the OKI limit.\n(3) No fuse on 12V input yet."
		(at 20.32 19.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
